From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:39:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 309/342] arp: the link-up announcements wait for a DHCP client
 to finish

A DHCP client asks for its address again when the link comes back, and until
it has it the interface is IFF_CONFIGURING: the announcements went out before
the address was there, or not at all. They wait now, up to 30 seconds, and
announce the address the client ends up with.

On the board with the RTL8812BU: link up, three waits of a second, the DHCP
acknowledgement, then the three announcements of the new address.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp     | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
index 34ba23166e..e770983f04 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@ struct arp_protocol : net_datalink_protocol {
 	in_addr_t	local_address;
 	net_timer	announce_timer;
 	int32		announcements_left;
+	int32		announce_waits;
 };
 
 
@@ -983,6 +984,14 @@ arp_announce_timer(struct net_timer* timer, void* data)
 		|| (interface->device->flags & IFF_LINK) == 0)
 		return;
 
+	// A DHCP client asks for the address again after a link came back: the
+	// announcements are for the address it ends up with.
+	if ((interface->flags & IFF_CONFIGURING) != 0) {
+		if (++protocol->announce_waits < 30)
+			sStackModule->set_timer(&protocol->announce_timer, 1000000);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	net_interface_address* address = NULL;
 	while (sDatalinkModule->get_next_interface_address(interface, &address)) {
 		if (address->local == NULL || address->local->sa_family != AF_INET)
@@ -1031,6 +1040,7 @@ arp_init_protocol(net_interface* interface, net_domain* domain,
 	sStackModule->init_timer(&protocol->announce_timer, arp_announce_timer,
 		protocol);
 	protocol->announcements_left = 0;
+	protocol->announce_waits = 0;
 
 	*_protocol = protocol;
 	return B_OK;
@@ -1188,6 +1198,7 @@ arp_control(net_datalink_protocol *_protocol, int32 op, void *argument,
 		// RFC 5227 announces twice, 2 seconds apart; the first one here waits
 		// a second for a wireless link's keys, and a third goes for luck
 		protocol->announcements_left = 3;
+		protocol->announce_waits = 0;
 		sStackModule->set_timer(&protocol->announce_timer, 1000000);
 		return B_OK;
 	}
